
It's weird seeing the school year start up again. Everything goes back to how it was before we left. Each year from now new people will be there, old people will leave, and no matter how homey that place used to feel, in a few years, it will be a complete stranger to you.

Life in this new place has settled to a happy cycle. I've found more connection to people at work than I thought, bonding over social deduction games. The end of the summer came in before it felt like it should, and it felt strange saying goodbyes to new friends so soon after I said goodbye to old ones. Wushu has been less friendly than I imagined. I'm starting to question my motivations for doing wushu. Part of it is a lack of goals; there's no collegiates to work towards. But maybe part of the joy of wushu is having people to share your progress with, people who care about your progress and thus you feel motivated to live up to it. 